# Playwright Rules

These rules apply to all Playwright tests in TennisConnect.

---

# General Principles

Tests must be:

- Independent
- Deterministic
- Readable
- Stable
- Fast
- Easy to debug

Avoid flaky tests.

---

# Test Structure

Every test must follow the same structure.

Example:

// ---------- Login ----------

// ---------- Verify login ----------

// ---------- Test data ----------

// ---------- Open page ----------

// ---------- Actions ----------

// ---------- Save ----------

// ---------- Verify request ----------

// ---------- Reload ----------

// ---------- Final verification ----------

Always separate logical sections with comments.

---

# Naming

Test names must follow:

FEATURE-001 Description

Examples

AUTH-001 Player Registration

PROFILE-003 Edit Player Profile

PROFILE-007 Upload Avatar

ACCESS-002 Guest Cannot Open Admin

MESSAGES-004 Reply To Conversation

---

# Folder Structure

tests/

auth/

profile/

messages/

admin/

access/

security/

helpers/

fixtures/

setup/

Never mix unrelated tests.

---

# Helpers

Reuse helper functions.

Examples

login()

logout()

registerPlayer()

registerCoach()

completePlayerProfile()

completeCoachProfile()

Never duplicate login code.

---

# Selectors

Always prefer

data-testid

Example

```ts
page.getByTestId("save-profile")
```

Avoid

```ts
locator("div:nth-child(3)")
```

Avoid CSS selectors unless necessary.

---

# Waiting

Never use

```ts
waitForTimeout()
```

Use

```ts
waitForResponse()

waitForRequest()

waitForURL()

expect(locator).toBeVisible()
```

Wait for application state instead of time.

---

# Network Verification

When saving data always verify:

Request

Response

Payload

Example

```ts
const [request, response] = await Promise.all([
    page.waitForRequest(...),
    page.waitForResponse(...),
    saveButton.click(),
]);
```

Verify

```ts
expect(response.ok()).toBeTruthy();
```

Verify payload

```ts
const body = JSON.parse(request.postData()!);

expect(body.name).toBe(profile.name);
```

---

# Assertions

Group assertions logically.

Good

```ts
expect(body.name).toBe(...);
expect(body.country).toBe(...);
expect(body.age).toBe(...);
```

Avoid scattered assertions.

---

# Test Data

Generate unique data.

Example

```ts
const timestamp = Date.now();
```

Avoid hardcoded values that can collide.

---

# Reload Verification

Whenever data is saved:

Reload page

Verify persisted values

Example

```ts
await page.reload({
    waitUntil: "networkidle",
});
```

Never verify only before reload.

---

# Upload Tests

Verify

File selected

Upload request

Response

Image updated

Reload

Image persists

---

# API Verification

Whenever possible verify

HTTP Status

Request payload

Response body

UI

Database behavior (if applicable)

---

# Authentication

Always verify login before continuing.

Example

```ts
await expect(page).toHaveURL(/player/);
```

Never assume login succeeded.

---

# Error Handling

Verify

Validation

Error messages

Disabled buttons

Unauthorized access

404 pages

500 errors

---

# Security Tests

Include tests for

SQL Injection

XSS

Invalid input

Long strings

HTML tags

JavaScript injection

Special characters

Empty values

Unexpected file uploads

---

# File Upload Tests

Verify

Allowed image types

Large images

Invalid extensions

No file selected

Upload cancel

Image persists after reload

---

# Pagination Tests

Verify

Next page

Previous page

Page numbers

First page

Last page

URL updates

Scroll position

Mobile layout

---

# Responsive Tests

Verify

Desktop

Tablet

Mobile

Buttons

Cards

Menus

Pagination

---

# Comments

Always use readable section comments.

Good

```ts
// ---------- Login ----------

// ---------- Save ----------

// ---------- Reload ----------

// ---------- Verify ----------
```

Avoid unnecessary comments.

---

# Debugging

Temporary debugging

```ts
console.log(body);

console.log(response.status());

console.log(await response.text());
```

Remove debug logs before merge unless useful.

---

# Code Style

Prefer

```ts
const saveButton = ...
```

Instead of

```ts
page.getByTestId(...).click();
```

Store locators in variables.

---

# AI Instructions

When generating Playwright tests:

- Follow existing TennisConnect style.
- Reuse helpers.
- Prefer data-testid.
- Keep sections readable.
- Verify UI and API together.
- Verify request payload.
- Verify response.
- Reload after save.
- Prefer stable assertions.
- Keep tests deterministic.
- Never use arbitrary timeouts.
- Generate production-ready automation.

---

# TennisConnect Standards

Every important CRUD test should verify:

✓ Login

✓ Open page

✓ Edit

✓ Save

✓ API request

✓ API response

✓ Request payload

✓ UI updated

✓ Reload

✓ Data persisted

This is the standard for all TennisConnect Playwright tests.
